        <body>
            <div xml:id="d168">

                <pb facs="0288" n="186" xml:id="pg186"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5896: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-18T10:00:00+08:00">February 18, 1933—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 18—4:36 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>160. Following from American Consul at Nanking: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“February 17, 11 a.m. I have been reliably informed that on the evening
                            of February 16 some Japanese official called at the Foreign Office and
                            inquired whether it was true that China intended to withdraw the Chinese
                            Minister to Japan. Vice Minister Hsu Mo replied that this would depend
                            upon the actions of Japan. (I asked Lo same question last night and he
                            gave me the same answer.) Vice Minister is reported to have asked the
                            Japanese official whether Japan was going to invade Jehol to which the
                            reply was that this appeared to be the orders from Tokyo. Asked whether
                            Japanese would take action inside the Wall the Japanese official replied
                            this would depend on needs of military strategy.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
